      "writtenOn": "2024-11-15T03:11:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e  I don\u0027t know if it will cause issues for example in the wire.\n\nOh I don\u0027t think you need to worry about it as both dawn_unittests and dawn_end2end_tests are running with dawn wire on the bots, \n\nActually `\"optional\": true` is applied to every item in the array instead of the pointer to the array.\n\nFor example, in ClientBase_autogen.h:\n\n----------------\n\nWith `\"optional\": true`:\n\nfor (decltype(memberLength) i \u003d 0; i \u003c memberLength; ++i) {\n    WIRE_TRY(provider.GetOptionalId(record.bindGroupLayouts[i], \u0026memberBuffer[i]));\n}\n\nWhere `provider.GetOptionalId()` will set `memberBuffer[i]` to 0 when `record.bindGroupLayouts[i]` is `nullptr`.\n\n----------------\n\nWithout `\"optional\": true`:\n\nfor (decltype(memberLength) i \u003d 0; i \u003c memberLength; ++i) {\n    WIRE_TRY(provider.GetId(record.bindGroupLayouts[i], \u0026memberBuffer[i]));\n}\n\nWhere `provider.GetId()` will return `WireResult::FatalError` when `record.bindGroupLayouts[i]` is `nullptr`.",
      "parentUuid": "58814df9_7e367bdb",
      "revId": "362d981e27974eb6bd8928e6818923a2f38ad5f9",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
